    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests run, 0 failures/errors. (The acceptance module is the only test class in the project.)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when the request omits `registrationDate`, it defaults to the server's current date; a supplied date is kept. The value is returned as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nKept structural impact low by extending existing units rather than adding new classes/steps \u2014 the OfficeFloor POST pipeline and the mapper are unchanged (MapStruct maps the new field by name automatically). Five files touched, no new function classes, and the one code method I grew (`BuildOwner.service`) sits in a class with almost no surrounding complexity:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's a writable input and flows into the `Owner` output DTO. The generated DTO field is a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field with `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")` plus a getter/setter (needed for JPA persistence and MapStruct mapping).\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema is authoritative; this matches the repo's precedent where the `email` column lives only in the hsqldb schema).\n- **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended the new positional value to the 10 seed owner rows so their inserts still match the widened table.\n- **`function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to an `Owner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when null (cohesive with this step's \"build the owner from the body\" role).\n\nThe GET response already serializes the entity through the same mapper, so `$.registrationDate` comes back automatically with no changes to the read path.",
